<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">22 August in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">9 events that happened on 22 August, from 851 to 1963.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/erispoe" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/erispoe.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/851">851 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">1,175 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Erispoe's Bretons defeat Charles the Bald at Jengland</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Near Grand-Fougeray on the border of Brittany, the Breton army of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/erispoe">Erispoe</a> defeated the West Frankish king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-the-bald">Charles the Bald</a>. By the Treaty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/angers">Angers</a> that followed, Charles recognised Erispoe as ruler of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bretons">Bretons</a>, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rennes">Rennes</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nantes">Nantes</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-jengland">Battle of Jengland</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-the-bald">Charles the Bald</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-francia">West Francia</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1138">1138 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">888 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">English forces defeat David I of Scotland at the Battle of the Standard</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Northern English levies rallied round a cart bearing a ship's mast and sacred banners near Northallerton and routed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/david">King David</a> I's army. It was a key battle of the civil war period known as the Anarchy.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1153">1153 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">873 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Baldwin III takes Ascalon from Fatimid Egypt</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After a siege begun in January, the Fatimid fortress of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ashkelon">Ascalon</a> surrendered to an army of crusaders, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/knights-templar">Templars</a> and Hospitallers under King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baldwin-iii-of-jerusalem">Baldwin III of Jerusalem</a>. It had been the last coastal city in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palestine">Palestine</a> outside crusader control.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baldwin-iii-of-jerusalem">Baldwin III of Jerusalem</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-jerusalem">Kingdom of Jerusalem</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fatimid-caliphate">Fatimid Caliphate</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1485">1485 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">541 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Henry Tudor defeats and kills Richard III at Bosworth</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/richard-iii-of-england">Richard III</a> was killed fighting at Bosworth Field when Lord Stanley's forces turned against him. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-vii-of-england">Henry Tudor</a> took the crown as Henry VII, founding the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-tudor">Tudor dynasty</a>.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1642">1642 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">384 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Charles I raises the royal standard at Nottingham</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After negotiations proved futile, King Charles I raised the royal standard in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nottingham">Nottingham</a>, beginning the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-english-civil-war">First English Civil War</a>. His forces controlled roughly the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/midlands">Midlands</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wales">Wales</a>, the West Country and the north; Parliament held <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a>, the south-east and the navy.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-english-civil-war">First English Civil War</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-i-of-england">Charles I</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nottingham">Nottingham</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1777">1777 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">249 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Benedict Arnold's ruse ends the siege of Fort Stanwix</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Benedict Arnold, then fighting for the Continental Army, convinced the British by a ruse that a much larger force was arriving, and Brigadier General Barry St Leger abandoned the siege of Fort Stanwix in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mohawk-river">Mohawk River</a> Valley.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/american-revolutionary-war">American Revolutionary War</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1864">1864 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">162 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The first Geneva Convention is signed</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Twelve states signed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/geneva">Geneva</a> Convention protecting wounded soldiers and the medical staff caring for them. It grew out of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-dunant">Henry Dunant</a>'s campaign and founded modern humanitarian law.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1902">1902 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">124 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Cadillac Automobile Company is founded in Detroit</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Investors reorganised Henry Ford's former company as Cadillac, named after the founder of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/detroit">Detroit</a>. Engineer Henry Leland's precision manufacturing made it a byword for quality.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1963">1963 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">63 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Joseph Walker flies the X-15 to the edge of space</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">NASA pilot Joseph Walker took the X-15 rocket plane to 107.8 km, beyond the 100 km boundary of space. The record for a winged aircraft stood until SpaceShipOne in 2004.</p></div></li></ol>
